{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scaleUnits","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"by","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"factor","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12XestiNumbers6NumberV","text":"Number","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"anchor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTiming8BeatTimeV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming\/BeatTime","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BeatTime"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"factor","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The factor to multiply each unit by.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"anchor","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The beat time from which units are scaled."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming\/UsingIvorTiming"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this after augmenting or diminishing the music from ","type":"text"},{"code":"anchor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by ","type":"text"},{"code":"factor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", to keep its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sound: each tempo keeps its rate, and its speed in whole notes per minute scales with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"music. For example, ♪ = 240 becomes ♩ = 240 when the music is augmented by 2.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing before "},{"code":"anchor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" changes speed. Unless "},{"code":"anchor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is zero, an unscaled entry is first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inserted at "},{"code":"anchor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", holding the tempo the music reaches there (the end of any ramp that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"runs into it). It comes before any entry already at ","type":"text"},{"code":"anchor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the speed steps there.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Then every other entry at or after ","type":"text"},{"code":"anchor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has its unit scaled. If no entry was at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"anchor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a scaled entry holding the tempo in effect there is inserted as well. That","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"includes ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming\/TempoMap\/defaultTempo","type":"reference"},{"text":", when this tempo map is empty.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inserting an entry inside a ramp splits it. The first part keeps its exact shape; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second becomes a fresh ease-in from the speed at "},{"code":"anchor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the ramp’s end, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"close to the original but not identical."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"factor"},{"type":"text","text":" is a positive rational number."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming","doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming\/TempoMap"]]},"s